course: dictionary
lesson: 16062
title: A grown-up drink
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things that only grown-ups use. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «The sign on the shop door said: vodka, adults only.» The words adults only are the clue. Vodka is for grown-ups, not children.
explain: «The bottle looked like water, but it was vodka.» The clues are looked like water and clear. Vodka is a clear liquid that looks like water, but it is not water. Vodka is a noun: it is the name of a thing.
explain: Vodka is a strong alcoholic drink, and alcohol can make people very ill. Children must never drink it, taste it, or touch an open bottle. If you find one, tell a grown-up you trust straight away.
fact: Vodka is a strong, clear alcoholic drink.
fact: Vodka was first made in Russia and Poland.
fact: Vodka is made from grain or potatoes.
fact: Vodka is for adults only, and children must never drink it.
fact: Alcohol like vodka can make people very ill.
exercise: «The shop sells vodka only to adults.» Who is vodka for? | Babies | *Grown-ups | Children
exercise: «The bottle looked like water, but it was vodka.» What is vodka? | Sweet fizzy lemonade | *A strong, clear alcoholic drink | A thick brown soup
exercise: Vodka was first made in Russia and Poland. Which two countries first made vodka? | Australia and Japan | *Russia and Poland | Brazil and Egypt
test: Why must children never drink vodka? | *It can make people very ill | It tastes of chocolate | It is too cold to drink
test: Find the word in «The bottle looked like water, but it was vodka.» that helps you know vodka is clear. | vodka | was | bottle | *water
exam: Vodka is made from grain or potatoes. Which of these is something vodka is made from? | Milk | Chocolate | *Potatoes | Sand
